let & const in JS

way of declaring variables in JS

let
Advantage of using let as below:

a. Prevent early access of the varaibale means variable call before declaration or defination is not possibe
console.log(name)
let name = "Shruti"  -> not possible

b. Restrict usage of vaiable out of block, if variable called out of block can not be access
for(let i=0;i<5;i++)
{} console.log(i) - > not allowed

c. can not redeclare variable
let address ='mumbai' let address = 'mumbai'

